From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: smit1237 <smit1237@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 00:33:47 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 29/30] rnsd: create the transport identity before the first
 start

On a first boot rnsd writes its transport identity only once it has
finished starting, many seconds in when the uplinks are unreachable. An
RNS client attaching meanwhile (rnstatus, the portal Reticulum tab)
found no identity, created its own and saved it over rnsd's, so every
client then got "digest received was wrong" until rnsd restarted.
S82rnsd now creates it with RNS before rnsd's first launch, so rnsd and
every client load the same file. Verified on the board.
---
 .../cvitek/SG200X/overlay/etc/init.d/S82rnsd  | 20 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)

diff --git a/buildroot/board/cvitek/SG200X/overlay/etc/init.d/S82rnsd b/buildroot/board/cvitek/SG200X/overlay/etc/init.d/S82rnsd
index fcf801c9f..2257c417a 100755
--- a/buildroot/board/cvitek/SG200X/overlay/etc/init.d/S82rnsd
+++ b/buildroot/board/cvitek/SG200X/overlay/etc/init.d/S82rnsd
@@ -317,6 +317,26 @@ start() {
 		rm -f "$LL_MARK"
 	fi
 
+	# First boot: create the transport identity before rnsd's first launch.
+	# rnsd itself writes it only once it has finished starting (after its
+	# interfaces, i.e. many seconds on a first boot with unreachable uplinks),
+	# and an RNS client that attaches meanwhile (rnstatus, the portal's
+	# Reticulum tab) finds no identity, creates its own and saves it over
+	# rnsd's: every client then derives the wrong RPC key ("digest received
+	# was wrong") until rnsd restarts. Created here, rnsd and every client load
+	# the same file. RNS's own generator, so the format always matches.
+	ident="$CFG_DIR/storage/transport_identity"
+	if [ ! -s "$ident" ]; then
+		mkdir -p "$CFG_DIR/storage"
+		if ( umask 077; python3 -c 'import sys, RNS; RNS.Identity().to_file(sys.argv[1])' "$ident" ) \
+			</dev/null >/dev/null 2>&1 && [ -s "$ident" ]; then
+			logger -t S82rnsd -p daemon.notice "created the transport identity before rnsd's first start" 2>/dev/null
+		else
+			rm -f "$ident"
+			logger -t S82rnsd -p daemon.warning "could not pre-create the transport identity; rnsd creates it" 2>/dev/null
+		fi
+	fi
+
 	# No rnsd is running. If the last one exited on its own (S46wanwatch's kick
 	# after a crash, say), end what it left running before its number in
 	# $PIDFILE is overwritten below - the only record of it.
-- 
